WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.310
Viserys Targaryen: The days of the Andals
were numbered.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:12.209
One by one, their so-called kings were bending
the knee or facing the wrath of Aegon Targaryen.

00:00:12.209 --> 00:00:16.610
Aegon of Old Valyria, Aegon, who was "blood
of the dragon."

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:22.090
Theon Greyjoy: When Aegon came demanding fealty,
King Harren the Black ruled as far east as

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.090
the Trident.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:28.961
Yara: Other kings, like the Starks, could
kneel, but Harren was ironborn, and the ironborn

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:31.390
must be beaten.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.680
In Harrenhal, he had the mightiest castle
in Westeros, and the army to defend it.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.380
Theon: But Aegon did not intend a siege.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.630
He mounted his dragon and roasted Harren and
all his sons in their tower, and the old way

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.450
with them.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.530
Because of Harren's defiance, Aegon pushed
the Ironborn back to our islands and gave

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.250
the Riverlands to the Tullys.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.790
But he did allow the ironborn to choose who
would lead them.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:01.420
Brynden Tully: The old River Kings, Storm
Kings, and the Kings of the Rock spilled blood

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:07.320
here for thousands of years, squabbling like
children over a new toy.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.080
Until the ironborn came and spanked them with
their axes.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.720
Under Harren the Black, their kingdom stretched
all the way to the Gods Eye, where they built

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.000
the largest castle Westeros had ever seen.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.990
Maesters teach that Harren was a fool, but
he had some sense.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:31.640
If you're going to enslave and torture an
entire people, you best have thick walls to

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.690
hide behind.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:41.260
But the very day the last stone was laid in
Harrenhal, Aegon Targaryen landed in Westeros.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:47.630
Euron Greyjoy: Harwyn Hoare, born to a king
who had a fleet he didn't sail, and swords

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:48.940
he didn't blood.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:55.141
As an unruly and worthless youngest son, Harwyn
was sent away to the east to vanish, and so

00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:56.340
he did.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:02.700
But when his father died, Harwyn returned
to the Iron Islands for the kingsmoot.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.631
An elder brother objected so an elder brother
fell off a horse, and at the kingsmoot, no

00:02:07.631 --> 00:02:09.060
man objected.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.379
Harwyn launched his father's ships for Westeros
and took ten times the Iron Islands from its

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:21.079
weak lords who never expected to face an ironborn
king as skilled on land as at sea.

00:02:21.079 --> 00:02:26.769
For Harwyn had reaved with eastern pirates
and served with eastern sellswords and learned

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:31.389
more of war than the ironborn could imagine.

00:02:31.389 --> 00:02:36.859
After Aegon and his dragons burned our last
king, Harren the Black, and broke our armies,

00:02:36.859 --> 00:02:43.540
the defeated ironborn chose my ancestor, Vickon
Greyjoy, as Lord of the Iron Islands, not

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.540
king.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:50.489
Robert Baratheon: House Baratheon was born
in the Wars of Conquest when Aegon the Dragon

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:53.329
invaded Westeros.

00:02:53.329 --> 00:02:58.169
Aegon sent his commander, Orys Baratheon,
to take Storm's End.

00:02:58.169 --> 00:03:03.919
Argilac the Arrogant, the last of the Storm
Kings, foolishly left the safety of his stronghold

00:03:03.919 --> 00:03:08.340
and met the Baratheon warlord in open battle.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:16.819
Argilac was soundly defeated, and Orys took
his lands, his holdings, and his daughter.

00:03:16.819 --> 00:03:19.700
Orys was said to be a half-brother to Aegon
Targaryen.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:27.049
If this were true, a little blood of the dragon
mingled with that of the stag in those days.

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:35.340
The seat of House Baratheon is Storm's End,
a legendary keep raised in the Age of Heroes.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:40.680
It overlooks Shipbreaker Bay, where legend
has it that Durran, the first Storm King,

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:46.669
raised the keep with the aid of Bran the Builder
of House Stark, forging a centuries-long connection

00:03:46.669 --> 00:03:49.779
with the Stormlands and the North.

00:03:49.779 --> 00:03:54.269
After Aegon's conquest of the Seven Kingdoms,
the Baratheons remained loyal enough to the

00:03:54.269 --> 00:03:57.969
crown while Targaryen kings came and went.

00:03:57.969 --> 00:04:00.400
But loyalty has its limits.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.559
Viserys Targaryen: After defeating the ironmen
at Harrenhal and slaying the last of the Storm

00:04:05.559 --> 00:04:12.010
Kings, Aegon and his sisters, Rhaenys and
Visenya, set their sights on other prizes.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:17.169
The gold mines of the Rock and the fertile
lands of the Reach.

00:04:17.169 --> 00:04:22.960
King Loren Lannister of the Rock and King
Mern Gardener of the Reach foolishly thought

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:27.720
their combined armies could beat back the
Targaryen host.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:34.240
They rode forth together, their proud banners
flapping in the wind, and faced off against

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.360
Aegon in a vast golden field of wheat.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:43.919
The two kings commanded a massive force of
nearly sixty thousand and it appeared the

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:45.710
day was theirs.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:52.560
Until Aegon unleashed all three of his dragons,
for the first and only time.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:58.039
Each beast was named after the Valyrian gods
of Aegon's forefathers.

00:04:58.039 --> 00:05:02.720
Visenya rode Vhagar, whose fiery breath could
melt armor.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:10.000
Rhaenys rode Meraxes, whose jaws were big
enough to swallow a horse whole.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:16.590
The greatest of all was Balerion the Black
Dread, with fire dark as night and wings so

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:21.770
huge, whole towns were covered in shadow when
he flew overhead.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:26.470
This magnificent creature was ridden by Aegon
himself.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:31.740
Four thousand men were bathed in glorious
dragon flame that day, on what came to be

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.789
known as the Field of Fire.

00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:40.530
King Mern was among the dead, and House Gardener
died with him.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:46.360
His stewards, the Tyrells, surrendered his
ancestral stronghold of Highgarden to Aegon

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:52.419
and were appointed Lords Paramount of the
Reach and Wardens of the South.

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:58.289
When Loren Lannister witnessed Mern's fate,
he wisely bent the knee.

00:05:58.289 --> 00:06:02.699
Aegon spared Loren's life, and the Lannisters
were made Lords Paramount of the Westerlands

00:06:02.699 --> 00:06:04.440
and Wardens of the West.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:11.500
Margaery Tyrell: Unlike the Lannisters, Starks,
and Arryns, we were never kings in our own

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.500
right.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:17.520
House Gardener ruled the Reach since the Dawn
Age, and we were their stewards.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:23.580
While they warred to enrich their already
rich domain, we managed their castle of Highgarden.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.340
But then Aegon Targaryen landed with his dragons.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:31.090
Nobody knows why the Gardener King took the
field up against him.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:37.319
Anyone could see that a man who grows flowers
should beware a man who grows fire-breathing

00:06:37.319 --> 00:06:38.319
monsters.

00:06:38.319 --> 00:06:41.280
But maybe it wasn't wholly his idea.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.810
Maybe someone whispered in his ear about all
the face he would lose with the other six

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:48.479
kings if he stayed home.

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:49.479
The rest is history.

00:06:49.479 --> 00:06:55.729
The last Gardener King lost his face, along
with his body, and his steward Harlen Tyrell

00:06:55.729 --> 00:06:58.870
promptly yielded Highgarden to Aegon.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:03.409
My grandmother swears that Harlen was like
most of our men and grew up banging steel

00:07:03.409 --> 00:07:09.840
too loudly for thought to penetrate, but luckily
his wife had better sense.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:15.469
Whatever the case, in return for Harlen's
show of sense, Aegon proclaimed House Tyrell

00:07:15.469 --> 00:07:21.009
the lords of the Reach and Wardens of the
South, passing over all the other houses with

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:23.610
better claims.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:28.740
Some Great Houses call us upstarts, but the
truth is that while the Starks and Lannisters

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:34.409
fell to the Targaryens in defeat, House Tyrell
rose.

00:07:34.409 --> 00:07:39.669
For thousands of years, our family served
as loyal stewards to the Kings of the Reach.

00:07:39.669 --> 00:07:47.090
Until the last of their line unwisely burned
to death, resisting the Targaryen invaders.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:52.499
To save the Reach from a similar fate, we
yielded the castle of Highgarden to Aegon

00:07:52.499 --> 00:07:54.509
and his sisters.

00:07:54.509 --> 00:08:01.819
In gratitude, the Targaryens gave House Tyrell
dominion over the Reach, and we became lords

00:08:01.819 --> 00:08:05.710
of the castle in which, for generations, we
had served.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:12.070
Qyburn: When Aegon the Conqueror was earning
his name, House Hightower traded its loyalty

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:19.759
to the Gardeners for his confirmation of their
rights, welcoming him with open arms and open

00:08:19.759 --> 00:08:20.840
gates.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:26.159
Pycelle: House Hightower bent the knee to
Aegon to spare the city from his dragons.

00:08:26.159 --> 00:08:31.520
I would think such insinuations and insults
beneath even you, Qyburn.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:35.720
Then again, mockery of one's betters is the
trade of fools.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.780
Qyburn: I wouldn't know.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:43.040
Robb Stark: The Starks reigned as kings for
thousands of years, even withstanding the

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.400
invasion of the Andals.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:49.970
As the southern kingdoms fell, and the Children
of the Forest were driven away, the North

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:54.790
stood strong, maintaining its religious customs
and its way of life.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:59.700
Eventually, the reign of the Kings of Winter
came to an end with the coming of Aegon the

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.750
Conqueror.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.910
After Aegon and his dragons destroyed the
combined armies of the Reach and the Rock

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:12.030
at the Field of Fire, King Torrhen Stark bent
the knee and swore fealty to the Targaryen

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:18.050
dynasty in order to spare the destruction
of Winterfell and his people.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.370
He was forever after known as "the King Who
Knelt."

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:27.590
As a reward for his submission, Aegon named
Torrhen Lord of Winterfell and Warden of the

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:28.590
North.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:32.330
Catelyn Stark: Aegon the Conqueror arrived
in Westeros.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:36.630
House Arryn bent the knee to Aegon and his
dragons and were allowed to maintain their

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:42.930
control of the region as Lords Paramount of
the Vale and Wardens of the East.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:48.630
Varys: King's Landing is both a city and a
curse.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:52.120
Aegon the Conqueror was the first king to
land there.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:56.100
His first conquest, a tiny village at the
mouth of the Blackwater River, where he raised

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.080
a wooden fort.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:02.440
When it became clear that Aegon would earn
his title, people flocked to the fort and

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:04.670
renamed it "King's Landing" in his honor.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:10.790
The ploy succeeded, and Aegon chose King's
Landing for his capital over older and more

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:16.340
beautiful cities like Oldtown and anywhere
else.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:21.910
The currying of royal favor thus became the
foundation of the city, and blood its bricks.

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:26.950
Oberyn Martell: Eventually, after centuries
of courtship, House Martell got into bed with

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:28.700
the Targaryens.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:33.630
We took King Daeron II and his sister for
our own before they could take each other,

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.160
and six kingdoms became seven.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:39.870
Even now, I do not blame my ancestors.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:42.460
One look at those long silver locks.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:46.110
It is not every day a man gets to ride a dragon.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:49.640
Viserys Targaryen: Aegon's conquest was assured.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:55.070
In a short time, the so-called Seven Kingdoms
were melted down in the heat of the dragons'

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:59.620
flame and transformed into a single realm.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:09.040
Aegon would forever be known as Aegon the
Conqueror.

